  "objective": "1. To synthesise qualitative studies that examine the experiences and perceptions of children with      
  chronic non‐cancer pain and their families regarding chronic non‐cancer pain, treatments and services to inform the   
  design and delivery of health and social care services, interventions and future research.  2. To explore whether     
  our review findings help to explain the results of Cochrane Reviews of intervention effects of treatments for         
  children\'s chronic non‐cancer pain.  3. To determine if programme theories and outcomes of interventions match       
  children and their families' views of desired treatments and outcomes.  4. To use our findings to inform the          
  selection and design of patient‐reported outcome measures for use in chronic non‐cancer pain studies and              
  interventions and care provision to children and their families.  The review questions are: 1. How do children with   
  chronic non‐cancer pain and their families conceptualise chronic pain?  2. How do children with chronic non‐cancer    
